<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Liberius (praetorian prefect)</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">c. 465–554</span> · <a href="/centuries/6th-century">6th century</a> · Also known as Petrus Marcellinus Felix Liberius</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Liberius was a Roman aristocrat and official who served <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/odoacer">Odoacer</a>, the Ostrogothic king Theodoric and finally the emperor Justinian. He was praetorian prefect of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/italy">Italy</a> and then of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/gaul">Gaul</a>, and later governed <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/egypt">Egypt</a> for Justinian. In 552, already in his eighties, he led the expedition that landed in south-eastern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hispania">Hispania</a> and began the Byzantine province of Spania.</p></div>
